{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowCorners","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.YoungLatticeUpOperator","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.BallotNumbers","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableauBot","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.TwoRowDimCatalan"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.numSYT_twoRow_eq_dimHLF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.numSYT_twoRow_eq_dimHLF","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowSYTBallot.lean#L212-L234","doc":"**The two-row tableau COUNT equals the hook-length-formula VALUE**, at general `m, k`.\n\nThis is the bridge the corpus was missing.  `dimHLF l := (sz l).factorial / prodHooks l` is the\nhook length *formula*; `numStandardYoungTableaux μ := Nat.card (StandardYoungTableau μ)` is the\ngenuine *count*.  Frame–Robinson–Thrall — the theorem that the two agree for **every** shape — is\nabsent from Mathlib and is proved in this corpus only for `n ≤ 4` (by `decide`) plus `n = 5`.\n\nFor **two-row** shapes it needs none of that: both sides were already identified with the same\nballot number, one side in August (`QOU.Mathlib.dimHLF_two_row_eq_ballot`) and the other by\n`numSYT_twoRow_eq_ballot` above, so composing the two identifications suffices at general `m, k`.\n\nCited by `QOU.Mathlib.TwoRowDimCatalan`'s module docstring, whose claim that\n`dimHLF_two_row_sq_sum` is \"a statement about actual standard-Young-tableau counts\" is true\n**because of this theorem** — before it, that file's `dimHLF` was a formula value with no proved\ntie to any tableau count at general `n`.\n\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] bean qou-7vht item 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.numSYT_twoRow_eq_ballot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.numSYT_twoRow_eq_ballot","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowSYTBallot.lean#L180-L210","doc":"**The two-row standard-tableau count IS the ballot number**, for every `k ≤ m`.\n\n    #SYT (m, k) = ballot (m + k) k\n\nOuter induction on `k`, inner induction on `m` from `k` upward (`Nat.le_induction`): the `k < m`\nstep needs the result at the *same* `k` with a smaller `m`, which an induction on `k` alone\ncannot supply.\n\nThe two `ballot` facts consumed are exactly the two the corpus already had: `ballot_succ_succ`\nfor the generic step, and `ballot_boundary_zero` for the `k = m` boundary, where the term that\nmust vanish is `ballot (2j+1) (j+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.numSYT_twoRow_rec_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.numSYT_twoRow_rec_eq","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowSYTBallot.lean#L168-L176","doc":"**`k = m > 0`: only the row-1 corner.**  `(0, m-1)` is *not* removable here — the cell below\nit is present — which is exactly what makes the boundary case work. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.numSYT_twoRow_rec_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.numSYT_twoRow_rec_lt","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowSYTBallot.lean#L156-L166","doc":"**`0 < k < m`: two corners.**  Successor form: `k = j + 1`, `m = M + 1`, `j + 1 ≤ M`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.numSYT_twoRow_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.numSYT_twoRow_zero","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowSYTBallot.lean#L143-L154","doc":"**One row, one tableau.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.twoRow_zero_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.twoRow_zero_zero","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowSYTBallot.lean#L135-L141","doc":"`twoRow 0 0` is the empty diagram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.eraseCornerOrSelf_twoRow_row1_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.eraseCornerOrSelf_twoRow_row1_succ","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowSYTBallot.lean#L126-L128","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.eraseCornerOrSelf_twoRow_row0_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.eraseCornerOrSelf_twoRow_row0_succ","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowSYTBallot.lean#L122-L124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.eraseCornerOrSelf_twoRow_row1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.eraseCornerOrSelf_twoRow_row1","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowSYTBallot.lean#L98-L113","doc":"Erasing the end of row 1 shortens row 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.eraseCornerOrSelf_twoRow_row0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.eraseCornerOrSelf_twoRow_row0","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowSYTBallot.lean#L81-L96","doc":"Erasing the end of row 0 shortens row 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.sum_cornerTwoRow_expand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.sum_cornerTwoRow_expand","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowSYTBallot.lean#L72-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.cornerCells_twoRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.cornerCells_twoRow","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowSYTBallot.lean#L67-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.mem_cornerTwoRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.mem_cornerTwoRow","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowSYTBallot.lean#L62-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.cornerTwoRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot.cornerTwoRow","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/TwoRowSYTBallot.lean#L58-L60","doc":"The removable corners of `twoRow m k`.  Mirrors `addableTwoRow`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}